  "steps": [
    {
      "text": "Soak couscous: Put the couscous and chermoula seasoning in a large heatproof bowl, add 1 tbs olive oil, pour over 200ml boiling water and cover with a plate. Stand for 5 mins or until the water is absorbed. Season with salt and pepper, then fluff the couscous with a fork.",
      "imageUrl": "https://marleyspoon.com/media/recipe_card_steps/2306514/photos/large/266468_1-499a8467ac3bb15c7bc92a7b9bf8229f.jpeg"
    },
    {
      "text": "Prep ingredients: Meanwhile, slice the haloumi. Coarsely chop the tomato.",
      "imageUrl": "https://marleyspoon.com/media/recipe_card_steps/2306524/photos/large/266468_2-7a4813034d7dddfa8ba6006b27fd1df5.jpeg"
    },
    {
      "text": "Cook haloumi: Heat a drizzle of olive oil in a medium frypan over medium-high heat. Cook the haloumi for 2 mins each side or until golden. Remove the pan from the heat.",
      "imageUrl": "https://marleyspoon.com/media/recipe_card_steps/2306529/photos/large/266468_3-2c58eb29d3998115e8ac9b804a063ea5.jpeg"
    },
    {
      "text": "Toss salad: Add the haloumi, tomato, rocket and 1 tbs white wine vinegar to the couscous and gently toss to combine.",
      "imageUrl": "https://marleyspoon.com/media/recipe_card_steps/2306532/photos/large/266468_4-67748553711fa9d215a8955141720ff9.jpeg"
    },
    {
      "text": "Serve up: Divide the couscous salad among bowls, scatter over the sunflower seeds and enjoy!",
      "imageUrl": "https://marleyspoon.com/media/recipe_card_steps/2306535/photos/large/266468_5-5ee6b0c70f3ef80250ea13bfc891742f.jpeg"
    },
    {
      "text": "Did you know: Although it looks like a grain, couscous is actually a type of pasta made from semolina flour and water. North African in origin, couscous means 'well rolled', named for the traditional way of making it – the semolina was sprinkled with water and then rolled by hand into tiny balls.",
      "imageUrl": "https://marleyspoon.com/media/recipe_card_steps/2306539/photos/large/266468_6-6008943387a372362a097cc2b5e7fe2e.jpeg"
    }
  ]
